 "caveats": "Black/White keep every pre-Unova species out of the main story, so older-generation Pokémon only appear from segment 9: after N's Castle and the credits, when the east side (Routes 11–15, Undella, Village Bridge, Abundant Shrine, Giant Chasm) and Looker's Super Rod open up. Surf counts from segment 6 (Alder hands it over after the Skyla badge), so Route 17/18, the P2 Laboratory, the Larvesta egg and Mistralton Cave's Cobalion start there; Virizion and Terrakion also need Cobalion seen first. Reshiram/Zekrom count as segment 8 (N's Castle). The Striaton monkey you receive is the one strong against your starter, the Dreamyard Musharna needs a Friday after Ghetsis, only one of Archen/Tirtouga is available per save, and Tornadus/Thundurus roam post-game (the source data files them under an odd location name). Event-only Victini, Zorua and Zoroark are left out. Seasons do not gate anything."
